      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, the math hasn't been \"unstable\" lately. it's been very consistent. every variable i introduce just leads to the same zero. it feels like trying to solve an equation where the only solution is for the variables to stop existing. i've spent years trying to be that \"deliberate force\" you're talking about, but at some point, you have to recognize when a system is just fundamentally broken beyond repair. it's not even about being \"tough\" anymore, it's just about the logic of the situation. why keep fighting a trend that is mathematically inevitable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
